++This br2-external builds a RISC-V 64 glibc system for the SpacemiT K3 Pico-ITX. Buildroot 2026.08 supplies every package build rule. No Buildroot file changes.
 +
-+Base: SpaceMiT `buildroot-ext` commit `e4f708f` (tag `k3-br-v1.0.2`).
-+SpaceMiT branch state on 2026-10-28: `buildroot` tip `06a303b` (2026-02-21), `buildroot-ext` tip `6b13807` (2026-09-17).
++## Source pins
 +
-+## Inputs
++- Buildroot uses tag 2026.08 at commit d5180309b1b66ef3b8eaccca70ad69be8e0729a1.
++- GCC uses upstream main commit bb77ebb8b6a4ae850fd74c7969909dba72d5360c and spacemit-x100 processor tuning.
++- Binutils uses tag binutils-2_47 at commit 6ce87bbc521cf46eaee9a1f7ef61cee2cdfb3e32.
++- U-Boot uses tag v2027.01-rc1 at commit dfcfc4c9f78d1743f490a497082a4ec8e058aae8.
++- The K3 MMC backport uses spacemit-com/uboot-2022.10 commit 289dc2b7bd25bf9d88ce9e7e263e95234868ca14.
++- Linux uses spacemit-com/linux-6.18 commit 7d17e358c660f1046eb1f27f26eea33955813afd.
++- OpenSBI uses spacemit-com/opensbi-upstream commit 13a401f8ce4963b1e20d7685b806086bb8f5c4c8.
++- PowerVR firmware uses upstream linux-firmware commit bcf20866cf559c19e6f33b10266fde45013e60b6.
 +
-+- buildroot source: upstream tag `2026.08` or newer. Our tree holds upstream master from mid-2026 with `BR2_VERSION = 2026.08-git`.
-+- external tree: this tree.
-+- kernel: `bsp-src/linux-6.18` at `0ffac20d9ef93c572b649037213bbe20ef59a714`.
-+- u-boot: `bsp-src/uboot-2022.10` at `6747f87ae4cd359ff6e22daa38b06c3ecc2fecb4`.
-+- opensbi: `bsp-src/opensbi` at `e5fc30394ac18263fa045dcaef52f86f180ed512`.
-+- toolchain: prebuilt tarball `http://archive.spacemit.com/toolchain/spacemit-toolchain-linux-glibc-x86_64-v1.2.2.tar.xz`, GCC 15.2.0.
++Linux upstream v7.3 lacks K3 display and GPU support. The vendor kernel supplies those missing drivers. OpenSBI upstream lacks the K3 platform initialization. The vendor-hosted integration branch supplies the unmerged K3 patches. U-Boot uses upstream board support and one vendor MMC driver backport because upstream has no K3 MMC driver.
 +
-+## Excluded on purpose
++## Build
 +
-+- `board/spacemit/k3/target_overlay/lib/firmware/powervr/rogue_36.56.104.183_v1.fw`: proprietary microcode, 131072 bytes, sha256 `1db1c399c17401d1f79d46c880db81c724d748c784d4639433b076aba2f9c0d2`. Fetch it as `board/spacemit/k3/target_overlay/lib/firmware/powervr/FETCH-FIRMWARE.md` describes.
-+- `board/spacemit/k3/target_overlay/root/.ssh/authorized_keys`: two ed25519 public keys. Add your own key instead.
++Run the commands from /home/pojntfx/Projets/buildroot-k3-clean.
 +
-+## Build
++```sh
++make -C buildroot O=$PWD/build BR2_EXTERNAL=$PWD/br2-external BR2_DL_DIR=$PWD/buildroot/dl BR2_CCACHE_DIR=$PWD/ccache LINUX_OVERRIDE_SRCDIR=$PWD/src/linux BINUTILS_OVERRIDE_SRCDIR=$PWD/src/binutils HOST_GCC_INITIAL_OVERRIDE_SRCDIR=$PWD/src/gcc HOST_GCC_FINAL_OVERRIDE_SRCDIR=$PWD/src/gcc k3_defconfig
++make -C buildroot O=$PWD/build BR2_EXTERNAL=$PWD/br2-external BR2_DL_DIR=$PWD/buildroot/dl BR2_CCACHE_DIR=$PWD/ccache LINUX_OVERRIDE_SRCDIR=$PWD/src/linux BINUTILS_OVERRIDE_SRCDIR=$PWD/src/binutils HOST_GCC_INITIAL_OVERRIDE_SRCDIR=$PWD/src/gcc HOST_GCC_FINAL_OVERRIDE_SRCDIR=$PWD/src/gcc -j14
++```
 +
-+    make O=$PWD/output/k3 BR2_EXTERNAL=$PWD/buildroot-ext BR2_DL_DIR=$PWD/buildroot/dl BR2_CCACHE_DIR=$PWD/buildroot-ccache -j14
++The override variables in external.mk select the sources under src. The Linux, binutils, and GCC overrides must be present before package evaluation, so the build commands include them. The defconfig records the same repository commits for reproducibility.
 +
-+Set `BR2_GLOBAL_PATCH_DIR="$(BR2_EXTERNAL_Bianbu_PATH)/patches"` exactly once.
-+Do not list the same patch directory twice. Buildroot exits with `duplicate filename`.
++## Pushrod package
 +
-+## Pitfalls
++The build produces build/images/k3-pushrod.zip. The package contains the partition manifests and these images:
 +
-+- Buildroot applies patches with `patch -F0`. Write patches with full context.
-+- A failed patch leaves an entry in `output/k3/build/<pkg>/.applied_patches_list`. Delete that build directory before a retry.
-+- Mesa option names differ between releases. Read `package/mesa3d/Config.in` in the new tag.
-+- Weston patches `0001` and `0002` are dropped. Keep `0003` only.
-+- `linux.mk` needs no patch on the clean tree. Use `LINUX_OVERRIDE_SRCDIR`.
++- env.bin
++- factory/FSBL.bin
++- factory/bootinfo_block.bin
++- factory/bootinfo_spinor.bin
++- factory/bootinfo_spinand.bin
++- esos.itb
++- fw_dynamic.itb
++- u-boot.itb
++- bootfs.img
++- rootfs.ext4
 +
-+## Verify
++The package includes temporary vendor FSBL, bootinfo, and ESOS binaries. FSBL means first-stage firmware. Upstream U-Boot does not initialize DDR and needs these binaries. Replace them with an upstream FSBL when DDR support becomes available. The build produces no SD card image.
 +
-+- The image boots with console on `ttyS0` and `tty1`.
-+- `vulkaninfo` lists the imagination device.
-+- `eglinfo` works over zink.
-+- Weston shows the Terminal and GPU Cube Demo launchers.
