++## Hardware state
++
++The board is in BROM at path 3-3-3-3-1-4. BROM is the boot ROM recovery mode. The relay board is /dev/hidraw11. Use /dev/ttyUSB1 for the working serial console. Buffer serial before every reset.
++
++The last fastboot query reported manufacturer DFU and productId 1001. Do not call flash.multiFlash or flash.flashFile in this mode. Those commands return OKAY but write nothing in BROM.
++
++## Pushrod access
++
++Use the MCP endpoint at http://127.0.0.1:1337/. The server restarted several times. Read initialize and tools/list before each hardware phase because its instructions can change.
++
++The built-in Pushrod binding was disconnected earlier. Direct JSON-RPC over HTTP worked. The endpoint is stateless and accepts tools/call requests with SSE responses.
++
++## Flash sequence
++
++1. Confirm the mode with flash.getDevices.
++2. Stage FSBL.bin only in BROM.
++3. Call flash.continue and read flash.getDevices again.
++4. Stage u-boot.itb.
++5. Call flash.continue and read flash.getDevices again.
++6. Read getvar:mtd-size and getvar:blk-size.
++7. Call flash.multiFlash with inline partition JSON objects and reboot true.
++
++Use partition_4M.json for a 4M MTD and partition_64M.json for a 64M MTD. Use partition_universal.json for universal block storage. Flash the MTD table first when both exist. Every partition already has name, offset, size, and image.
++
++If the BROM device disappears, run target.reset and target.enterFDL. Confirm the mode with flash.getDevices before staging anything.
