++
++Use KVM for a screenshot. Query kvm.getVideoCaptureDevices for the current path. A panel launcher needs a doubleClick.
++
++## Validation fixes for the new tree
++
++- Downstream U-Boot reads the FAT16 boot filesystem with 4K sectors. It does not read the current 1K ext4 boot filesystem.
++- Downstream U-Boot loads Image, k3-pico-itx.dtb, and env_k3.txt from the boot filesystem root. Set dtb_dir to an empty value in env_k3.txt.
++- The new device tree changes the remote processor reserved-memory layout. It causes a panic in spacemit_get_loaded_rsc_table with the current FSBL and firmware.
++- The old device tree avoids the remote processor panic. Keep the device tree, FSBL, and remote processor firmware memory layouts synchronized in the new tree.
++- The built-in PowerVR driver probes before the root filesystem mounts. Build CONFIG_DRM_POWERVR=m so the driver loads after root mounts.
++- The driver requests powervr/rogue_36.56.104.183_v1.fw, but the current linux-firmware pin lacks that file. The rootfs overlay now carries the required firmware from the old build.
++- PowerVR advertises linear tiling without the legacy sampled linear-filter feature. The Mesa patch adds that feature so Weston can create its DMA-BUF format table.
++- Renderer-owned DMA-BUFs use the direct-display path to avoid a redundant GBM reimport. Vulkan still renders into each buffer before KMS receives it.
++- Weston 15 rejects the --tty option. Select the connected DRM card, load /etc/weston.ini explicitly, and use the native Vulkan renderer.
++- The vendor k3_defconfig starts a debug initramfs shell. Set CONFIG_INITRAMFS_SOURCE="" so the kernel mounts the new rootfs directly.
++- The current boot configuration names /dev/mmcblk0p8 as the root filesystem. Use the rootfs PARTUUID or /dev/sda2 for UFS boot.
++
